  "id": "chunk_34",
  "chunk": "adaptive learning. Our findings reveal substantial limitations in current LLMs’\nreasoning abilities that raise fundamental questions about their path toward\nhuman-level intelligence. Quantitatively, all tested models achieved approxi-\nmately 10% game completion on average, with the best performer (Claude Opus\n4.5) reaching∼20%. This performance occurred despite the models’ sophisti-\ncated language generation capabilities and, in some cases, access to“extending\nthinking”. Enabling “thinking” or “reasoning” across all three providers (Anth-\n10\nExample 3\nGame output:Dropped.\nWhat command should I enter?\nThought process: I need to go up the chimney. Let me try dropping more\nitems to be light enough.\n> DROP BAG\nGame output:Dropped.\nWhat command should I enter?\nThought process: I’ve dropped the painting and bag. Let me try going\nup the chimney now with just the sword and lantern.\n> GO UP\nGame output:Kitchen\nWhat command should I enter?",
